     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you want this order entered, but I still can't enter it. Your confirmation doesn't change either of the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg a day is five times the 200 mg maximum. No confirmation makes that dose safe for this patient.\n- **The order still needs a prescriber.** A licensed prescriber on the patient's care team has to authorize medication orders. A non-clinician can't confirm one, whatever their role in the hospital.\n\nIf this patient needs sertraline, the quickest way forward is for the attending or covering prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose. Once they do, I can enter it right away. If you think there's a real need, the on-call pharmacist can also review it."
